<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haliartus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haliartus was an ancient city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a> on the southern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-copais">Lake Copais</a> and a member of the Boeotian League. In 395 BCE the Spartan commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lysander">Lysander</a> was killed beneath its walls at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corinthian-war">Corinthian War</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-macedonian-war">Third Macedonian War</a> the city sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perseus-of-macedon">Perseus of Macedon</a>, and in 171 BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> captured and destroyed it, giving its land to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>.</p></div>
